            "review_title": "Review at Cawa Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Ania Z\nMoscow, Russia68 contributions\n0\nOne of the best restaurants in Nha Trang\nApr 2026 • Couples\nOne of the best restaurants we've eaten on our entire vacation is Cawa Restaurant, a Mediterranean restaurant. We wandered into it completely by accident, even though it was close to our hotel, not on the way, but in an alley. Exact address: 96B Trần Phú, Lộc Thọ, Nha Trang. As a guide, you can use the Sadko Mysteries jewelry store and the Bath Mi bun tent, which is right on the corner next to the restaurant. We had lunch here three times and the room was always full. The restaurant looks simple but neat. The staff is polite and hasty, there is a Vietnamese girl who speaks very good Russian. Prices are low or medium, depending on the dish ordered. The first two times we took seafood and fish here, they were amazing. For the third time, they decided to try the delicacies and ordered ostrich meat and grilled crocodile meat. The ostrich wasn't bad, but the crocodile struggled to chew. Soup pho bo brightened this impression a little - boiled broth, lots of noodles, but the beef is tough again. The portions are really big, you can safely order one for two to try more dishes.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten April 27, 2026",
